      section: "CS",
      q: "An operating system uses the Banker's algorithm for deadlock avoidance when managing the allocation of three resource types X, Y, and Z to three processes P0, P1, and P2. Allocation / Max (X,Y,Z): P0: (0,0,1) / (8,4,3); P1: (3,2,0) / (6,2,0); P2: (2,1,1) / (3,3,3). There are 3 units of X, 2 units of Y and 2 units of Z still available. The system is currently in a safe state. Consider the following independent requests: REQ1: P0 requests 0 units of X, 0 units of Y and 2 units of Z. REQ2: P1 requests 2 units of X, 0 units of Y and 0 units of Z. Which one of the following is TRUE?",
      options: ["Only REQ1 can be permitted.","Only REQ2 can be permitted.","Both REQ1 and REQ2 can be permitted.","Neither REQ1 nor REQ2 can be permitted."],
